  "blurb": "A fully furnished resale villa high on the Bang Por hillside, where an infinity pool runs straight out toward the sea. Three en-suite bedrooms, open-plan living and a timber-slatted sala on 754 m² of land, with its own deep well for water self-sufficiency. ฿24,150,000 including a 30-year lease, with very good rental returns — figures on request.",
  "detail": "AN INFINITY POOL FACING THE SEA\nOn the hillside above Bang Por, on Koh Samui's north coast, this villa sits within a small community of contemporary pool villas looking out across the Gulf. It is offered as a resale, fully furnished and ready to move into or rent out.\n\nOUTDOOR LIVING\nThe infinity pool is the centrepiece, its edge disappearing into the sea view beyond. Around it are wide sun terraces, a barbecue area and a timber-slatted sala with deep cushioned seating and hanging egg chairs — shaded, breezy and looking straight out to sea.\n\nINSIDE\nOpen-plan living, dining and a sleek kitchen with a marble-look island open fully to the pool terrace. Three en-suite bedrooms and three and a half bathrooms, finished in pale oak, white walls and soft natural textures. Floor plans are at the end of the gallery.\n\nWATER SELF-SUFFICIENT\nThe villa has its own private deep well, so it does not depend on the island's water supply.\n\nOWNERSHIP\nLeasehold: the land is owned by a Thai owner, and a 30-year lease is included in the sale price.\n\nINVESTMENT\nThe villa offers very good rental returns; ROI figures are available on request.\n\nKEY FACTS\n3 en-suite bedrooms · 3.5 bathrooms\nBuilt area 350 m² · living area 256 m² (indoor + outdoor)\nLand 754 m² · Chanote title\nLeasehold — 30-year lease included in the price\nInfinity pool facing the sea · sala & terraces\nPrivate deep well — water self-sufficient\nFully furnished · resale\nPrice: ฿24,150,000",
